# Files that run inside a Linux container must keep LF endings.
#
# This checkout has core.autocrlf on, so without these a shell script arrives
# with CRLF and the container fails with a "bad interpreter" error that names
# no obvious cause - the script looks perfectly fine in an editor.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
